## How this repo is organized

The repo is split by how fast things change, so each folder has one lifecycle and one owner:

- `docs/` holds what is true now, grouped by reader: `dev/` for contributors and `user/` for end users (each with tutorials, how-to guides, reference and explanation), plus `decisions/` (ADRs) for everyone.
- `work/` holds what is happening now: work items, the human decision queue, research notes. Expected to be pruned.
- `agents/` holds how the work gets done: roles, protocols, and skills. Tool-neutral, so any agent can follow them.
- `tools/` holds small standard-library scripts that keep all of the above consistent.
- {% if layout == 'workspace' %}The code lives in `apps/` and `packages/`, tested in `tests/`.{% elif layout == 'data-ml' %}The code, datasets and notebooks live in `src/`, `data/` and `notebooks/`, tested in `tests/`.{% elif layout == 'minimal' %}Add your project or engine folders at the root, each with a `README.md` (`summary` and `owner_role`).{% else %}The code lives in `src/`, tested in `tests/`.{% endif %}

Full folder map: [docs/dev/reference/repo-map.md](docs/dev/reference/repo-map.md). Why it is built this way: [docs/dev/explanation/design-rationale.md](docs/dev/explanation/design-rationale.md).

## Everyday commands

```
python3 tools/check.py                    # is the repo healthy? (run before every handoff)
python3 tools/new_item.py <slug>          # start tracking a piece of work
python3 tools/check.py --stubs            # list unfilled placeholders
python3 tools/remove_module.py            # list optional modules you can cut
```

